        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Why is my XTERRA treadmill not turning on?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Check the safety key first, then the power switch and the circuit breaker on the front of the base, which you push in until it locks. Then check the wall outlet and your breaker panel. XTERRA's manuals ask for a grounded 120-volt, 15-amp outlet with no other appliances on the circuit.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What does E1 mean on an XTERRA treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It depends on the model. On the TR65, E1 means a missing speed signal, so check the speed sensor connection. On the TRX1000, TRX1200 and TR150, E1 appears 8 to 10 seconds after pressing Start, and the manual says to check whether the motor runs and the cable between the console and controller.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I reset my XTERRA treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Remove the safety key, turn the power switch off, unplug for about a minute, then plug in, switch on and replace the key. If it is completely dead, push in the circuit breaker on the front of the base. Pressing Stop twice also returns the console to its start-up screen.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I get rid of the LUBE message on my XTERRA?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Check the deck and lubricate it if it is dry. Then, on the TRX1000, TRX1200 and TR65, hold the PROGRAM key for 3 seconds in standby mode to clear the message. Some models, such as the TR75, reset it from the Engineering Mode menu instead.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How often should I lubricate an XTERRA treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Follow your model's manual. The TR65, TR75, TR95H and TRX1200 manuals say every 90 days or 90 hours, the TRX1000 manual says 80 hours, and XTERRA's FAQ says every 3 months or 180 hours. Lubricate sooner if the deck feels dry, and use only XTERRA-approved lubricant.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why does my XTERRA treadmill keep tripping the breaker?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Usually because something else shares the circuit, or because the deck is dry and the motor is working too hard. XTERRA's manuals say AFCI and GFCI breakers can trip from the treadmill's inrush current and recommend making the treadmill the only device on the circuit. Clean and lubricate the deck as well.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the XTERRA customer service number?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              XTERRA's website listed 870-336-4286, Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, on 24 November 2026. Have your model, the 16-character serial number from the frame near the power cord, and your proof of purchase ready.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

